{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1183","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1183","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1183\",\"parent_revision\":\"42204f18ebd93791ed5e7256dcdb517c30e82fc3\",\"root_revision\":\"c116ab47b5ac4d1042d11e6fc514cc63cf9d3e3362e10be1e3fab784ae5669e9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`work-backlog-item close` currently expects a title substring. Since GitHub Issues are now the canonical source of truth, `close #N` and `resolve #N` should also be valid \u2014 fetch the title from the issue and proceed. This eliminates the need to remember exact title substrings for the common case of closing work started with `/work-backlog-item #N`. Routing table in `SKILL.md` needs a new `#N` row for the close/resolve paths.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Routing table in `SKILL.md` | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` |\\n| 2 | `parse.mjs` parser script | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/parser/parse.mjs` |\\n| 3 | Close workflow that receives `item_ref` | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/close/start.md` |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all information available.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **work-backlog-item: accept `#n` in `close` and `resolve` routing** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #149 follow-up \u2014 start-milestone automation (2026-02-22)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Low complexity. Parser and routing table update only. No behavioral change for existing title-substring usage.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `work-backlog-item close #42` resolves issue #42 via GitHub, fetches the title, and proceeds with closure\\n- `work-backlog-item resolve #42` similarly accepts an issue number\\n- Routing table in `SKILL.md` updated with a `#N` row for close/resolve paths\\n- Parser script (`parse.mjs`) updated to extract issue number from `close #N` and `resolve #N` invocations\\n- Existing title-substring close/resolve behavior unchanged\\n- Test: `parse.mjs` output for `close #42` has `route: 'close'` and `item_ref: '#42'`\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 update routing table close/resolve rows\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/parser/parse.mjs` \u2014 handle `close #N` and `resolve #N` patterns\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a work-backlog-item user who tracks work by issue number, I need `close #N` and `resolve #N` to work as valid inputs so I can close items without remembering exact title substrings.\\n\",\"digest\":\"585da0e2ed8e1f0a429bd05c55a77aaae2c824f075f148f84abdcc0478e66604\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg5Msw\"}"}